course: dictionary
lesson: 5870
title: Mandate: permission given to act
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A mandate is permission to act, given by people who have the power to choose. In politics, voters give a government a mandate when they vote for its plans. «The party won a clear mandate at the election» means the voters backed what the party wanted to do.
explain: Mandate can also mean an official order. «A mask mandate» is a rule saying people must wear masks. Here the word means a rule that must be followed, not just a suggestion.
explain: As a verb, to mandate means to order something officially. The verb changes its ending: mandates, mandated, mandating. «The school mandated new reading tests.» The words around it, such as order and rule, help you check the meaning.
fact: A mandate is an authority or permission given to someone to act.
fact: «Mandate» can be a noun (a mandate) or a verb (to mandate something).
fact: «Mandatory» means required, so something mandatory must be done.
fact: «The Mandate of Heaven» was a belief in ancient China that Heaven gave a good ruler the right to rule.
fact: In that belief, «floods, famine and rebellion» showed a ruler had lost the Mandate, and people could replace him.
exercise: «The party won a clear mandate from the voters.» What does mandate mean here? | A rule that children must sing | A map of the country | A large, empty room | *Permission to act, given by voters
exercise: «A mask mandate means people must wear masks.» What does mandate suggest? | A type of mask | A nice suggestion you can ignore | *A rule that must be followed | A party game
exercise: What does mandatory mean? | Dangerous | *Required | Very old | Optional
test: «The Mandate of Heaven said a bad ruler could lose the right to rule.» What could a bad ruler lose? | His castle | *The right to rule | Money | His voice
test: The school mandated new rules, so every pupil must follow them. What does mandated mean? | Lost in the post | Painted in bright colours | *Ordered officially | Forgotten
exam: «The class gave Leo a mandate to speak for them at the assembly.» What does mandate mean here? | *Permission given by others to act for them | A loud shout | A school lunch | A seat at the back
